# NOTE: A new report comes out every October at https://www.globalhungerindex.org/xlsx/<year>.xlsx; bump the year in
#  url_download and citation_full. Besides the "GHI Scores <year>" sheet that we use, the file has a ranking sheet and a
#  sheet with the values of the four component indicators, which we do not ingest.
# Learn more at:
# http://docs.owid.io/projects/etl/architecture/metadata/reference/
meta:
  origin:
    # Data product / Snapshot
    title: "Global Hunger Index"
    description: |-
      The Global Hunger Index (GHI) is a tool designed to comprehensively measure and track hunger at global, regional, and national levels, reflecting multiple dimensions of hunger over time.

      Each country's GHI score is calculated based on a formula that combines four indicators that together capture the multidimensional nature of hunger:

      - Undernourishment: the share of the population whose caloric intake is insufficient;
      - Child stunting: the share of children under the age of five who have low height for their age, reflecting chronic undernutrition;
      - Child wasting: the share of children under the age of five who have low weight for their height, reflecting acute undernutrition; and
      - Child mortality: the share of children who die before their fifth birthday, reflecting in part the fatal mix of inadequate nutrition and unhealthy environments.

      The calculation results in GHI scores on a 100-point scale, where 0 is the best score (no hunger) and 100 is the worst.
    date_published: "2026-10-14"

    # Citation
    producer: "Welthungerhilfe et al."
    citation_full: |-
      Welthungerhilfe (WHH), Institute for International Law of Peace and Armed Conflict (IFHV), and Helvetas. 2026. 2026 Global Hunger Index: No Security Without Food Security. Bonn/Berlin: WHH; Zürich: Helvetas; Bochum: IFHV.

    # Files
    url_main: https://www.globalhungerindex.org/download/all.html
    url_download: https://www.globalhungerindex.org/xlsx/2026.xlsx
    date_accessed: 2026-11-12

    # License
    # NOTE: The site footer and the report name the "Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License", but link to
    #  CC BY-NC-ND 4.0.
    license:
      name: "CC BY 4.0"
      url: https://www.globalhungerindex.org/download/all.html

